' The user menu of Vibe Commander, which F2 shows: a line at the left
' margin is an item, a key and a colon and what the menu shows; the
' lines below it that begin with a space or a tab are its commands.
' A line that begins with an apostrophe is a comment. In a command,
' ! is the name of the file under the cursor, !.! the name with its
' extension, !: the current drive and !\ the current directory.
'
' A web page cannot run commands: an item here says so on DOS's
' screen, which Ctrl-O shows. Edit this file with Menu file edit, in
' the Commands menu, and try your own.
D: Show the date and the time
	date
	time
L: List the current directory
	dir !:!\
T: Type the file under the cursor
	type !.!
